  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He sits in a tree watching Ni Jian fight a brown bear he chose as an opponent, then tosses muddy Gu down so the boy can trap the beast. He asks whether Ni Jian now sees muddy Gu’s advantages and confirms he wants the grandson to give up sword path for Ni clan’s earth path specialty.",
      "chapters": [
        1034
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ni_jian",
        "fac_ni_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration names him Ni Jian’s grandfather, current leader of Ni clan, and a rank five Gu Master. When alert bell Gu rings he grabs Ni Jian and runs to the village at rank five speed, then uses the clan’s investigative Gu formation, sees a beast tide a hundred li away, and orders layered defenses, heavenly fire Gu formation, medicine hall, and youth evacuation.",
      "chapters": [
        1034
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-leader",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Zai learns that the Ni clan leader was the current generation Ni Xiang with yes or no Immortal Gu in his body. A mysterious Gu Immortal forced him to answer and promised to spare the village; he sacrificed himself to protect the clan, then the enemy broke the word and slaughtered the village.",
      "chapters": [
        1037
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qi_zai",
        "char_ni_xiang",
        "gu_yes_or_no_immortal_gu",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s earlier question to the current generation Ni Xiang about Fixed Immortal Travel and other Immortal Gu received No; after that one answer the old clan leader died on the spot from the fifty-year lifespan cost.",
      "chapters": [
        1039
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
